  "review": {
   "texts": [
    "good. parses faithfully — the one-day-before-equinox anchor, the Year 1 date, the store's location at Cauldron Hall, the stative holding with the store as doer and the supply as what is held, and the ten-week figure are all carried. The reviewer's two reservations are gaps in our own instruction set (no positive rule yet for a measure of-phrase like \"ten weeks of supply\"), not content your sentence lost.",
    "good. the reporting is a past event with Hesper as the reporter and the Council as the addressee, and the that-clause is sealed rather than asserted — correct, since reporting something does not make it so. The harvest's own typing is projected to top level so it stays queryable, and the past-perfect \"had been thin\" is kept inside the report."
   ]
  },
  "census": {
   "passage": "ok"
  }
 },
